{"xson":[{"/iati-activities/iati-activity":[{"/activity-date":[{"@iso-date":"2014-03-24","@type":"2"},{"@iso-date":"2023-12-31","@type":"4"}],"/activity-status@code":"4","/collaboration-type@code":"2","/contact-info":[{"/department/narrative":[{"1":"NEN","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/email":[{"1":"p.clos@ifad.org"}],"/job-title/narrative":[{"1":"Country Director","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/organisation/narrative":[{"1":"International Fund for Agricultural Development","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/person-name/narrative":[{"1":"Clos, Paul Edouard","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/telephone":[{"1":"+390654591"}],"/website":[{"1":"http://www.ifad.org"}],"@type":"1"}],"/default-aid-type":[{"@code":"C01","@vocabulary":"1"}],"/default-tied-status@code":"5","/description":[{"/narrative":[{"1":"Overall objective. The overall objective of the project is to improve living conditions for vulnerable rural people and create new opportunities for employment by strengthening the resilience of agropastoral production systems and the related value chains.Specific objective. The specific objective is for public and private actors to be able to manage and sustainably develop local territories and agropastoral value chains, including camelids and small ruminants. As room for improving agropastoral productivity remains circumscribed by ecoclimate constraints, investment will be oriented towards adding value at the various links in value chains, developing new local goods and services, and lowering costs by organizing actors.","@xml:lang":"EN"}]}],"/document-link":[{"/category":[{"@code":"A02"},{"@code":"A07"},{"@code":"A08"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrative":[{"1":"Tunisia 1100001704: PRODEFIL Supervision Report December 2021","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"@format":"APPLICATION/PDF","@url":"https://operations.ifad.org/documents/654016/a45c9c2f-e90e-47d8-b569-47c82a9a27ce"},{"/category":[{"@code":"A02"},{"@code":"A07"},{"@code":"A08"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrative":[{"1":"Tunisia 1100001704: PRODEFIL